  "title": "Das Gedaechtnis Der Eth Zuerich",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "Are you interested in exploring the history of ETH Zurich, or the life and works of prominent scientists such as Nobel Prize winners Albert Einstein or Vladimir Prelog? Then, the ETH Zurich University Archives are exactly the right place for you.\n\nThe team at the University Archives is responsible for securing, indexing and mediating important documents relating to ETH Zurich and the ETH Board, as well as managing scientific papers from former ETH members.\n\nGet to know the University Archives in a new video, and discover how its team can assist and advise you with a range of questions and concerns.\n\nWant to learn more? Visit the University Archives’ informative websites\n\n#KnowHow – ETH Library’s infrastructure and tools lead you to your goal."
    }
  ],
